/.qg-cache/
# Go/lint caches created by quality-gate runs and ad-hoc worker invocations.
# These are regenerable build artifacts, but an UNIGNORED one makes
# `git status --porcelain` non-empty, which the dispatcher reads as
# unpreserved work and quarantines as stale_active_assignment — that froze
# the factory on 2026-07-28. Patterns are unanchored and cover the per-bead
# suffixed forms (e.g. .gocache-oro-3zk9) seen in worker worktrees.
.gocache*/
.golangci-cache*/
.golangci-lint-cache/
.task-gocache/
# Cover the ENTIRE .qg-* family by prefix. Three narrower attempts each leaked:
# enumerated names missed .qg-affected-golangci-cache, and .qg-*cache* missed the
# randomized per-run scratch dirs the gate mints per lane+invocation
# (.qg-lint-1QyLYx, .qg-verify-lint-main-IZ8Rzy, .qg-recheck-go-UQiLDM) because
# those carry no "cache" in the name. That leak dirtied two worktrees and raised
# progress_timeout_recovery_blocked quarantine 449, idling the factory.
# The gate owns the .qg- prefix, so match on it rather than on any inner word.
# No trailing slash: the gate emits FILES too (.qg-incident-588-coverage.out),
# and a trailing-slash pattern matches directories only.
.qg-*
# Undotted forms nested under .oro/ — leading-dot patterns above miss these.
.oro/gocache/
.oro/golangci-cache/
**/dispatcher.exit.log
.gstack/
pkg/dispatcher/workers/
/.oro/context_pct
/.oro/review-pattern-candidates.md
/.oro/review-pattern-candidates.promoted.md
/.oro/state.sqlite

